WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.250
It's freaking gnarly, dude.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.150
It's as gnarly as I could
have imagined it being.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.200
This is a lot of fun.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.900
Just really nervous about
how fast I'm going to be

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.580
actually flying off the lip.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.990
With drop kayaking,
when you're really pushing

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.010
yourself is when
you feel more alive,

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.950
but it's really dangerous.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:31.310
Waterfall running is not
something that everybody

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.560
likes to engage with.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.960
You come in with speed,
and then you immediately

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.080
go to a vertical freefall.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.475
You are going from 45 miles
an hour to a dead stop.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.240
It feels like being
whiplashed in a car crash.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.230
We take hits.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:59.530
Hitting your face with your
paddle, breaking your nose,

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:03.470
which is why we sometimes
throw the paddles.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.750
The benefit of
throwing your paddle,

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.910
it creates less
chances of hitting

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:10.280
yourself with the paddle.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.330
With a hydraulic, you
have this curtain of water

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:15.800
that's hitting
the pool, and it's

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.370
pulling you down underwater.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:22.400
If you are in a hydraulic,
you can also play dead,

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.420
and then the water will pull
you down and pop you downstream.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.640
It's kinda sketchy out there.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.680
If you go too far right,
it has a really bad spot

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.162
where it kind of folds back
in and you would probably

00:01:38.162 --> 00:01:39.370
just break your boat and die.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:47.730
The Rio Santo Domingo has
this super steep section that

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:50.640
had never been done before as a
complete top-to-bottom descent.

00:01:53.676 --> 00:01:55.500
I get it.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.140
They're crazy-looking
rapids, man.

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:06.080
Before running a rapid, you
always visualize the line.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.520
How are you going to
enter the current?

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:15.280
Where are your reference points,
a rock or a breaking wave?

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.530
And where do you want
to be on that lip?

00:02:24.012 --> 00:02:26.470
I feel like we need a solid
safety team down there, dude.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:28.130
And the amount of people
that we have right now,

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.297
I'm not sure if it's enough.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.830
On trips like this, you have
to trust that your partners are

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.810
going to be able
to potentially save

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:42.630
your life because in
big drop kayaking,

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:46.350
you can plan every move,
you can scout every line,

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:49.470
but until you're in the
water, you don't know

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:50.775
exactly what's going to happen.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.910
The most important thing
for me is not getting hurt.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.800
I don't want that for my family.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:15.534
[NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:16.980
[BABY COOING]

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:19.641
[VOCALIZING]

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.062
How are you, buddy?

00:03:24.062 --> 00:03:25.460
ALI CASAS: [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.470
Hey, what you guys reading?

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.260
When I met Gerd,
I started kayaking.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.660
He's been a good
teacher, and we've been

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.660
kayaking together ever since.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:39.460
You got the keys?

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:40.990
ALI CASAS: Kayaking
gives you more

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:46.180
mental strength because
you're about to run

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.770
something that scares you.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.050
I trust him a lot,
and I know that he

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.340
doesn't do stupid things.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.020
But I worry all the time.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.660
I just don't tell him.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.320
Nice!

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.220
Let's go.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.860
You ready?

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.870
We have two tiny
persons at home

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:10.310
that they are waiting for
him, and you always think

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.930
that something bad can happen.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.880
[MUSIC PLAYING]

